From: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] kbuild: disable dangling-pointer false positives

Newer GCC versions diagnose temporary stack-backed list entries in semaphore
wait queues and memory compaction. Those entries are removed before their
stack frames return, but the compiler cannot track that lifetime across the
list helpers and scheduling operations.

Disable only this diagnostic, using the compiler capability check so older
GCC and Clang remain supported. Keep CONFIG_WERROR for other diagnostics.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [vendor kernel compiler compatibility]
Signed-off-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 Makefile | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -771,6 +771,7 @@ KBUILD_CFLAGS	+= $(call cc-disable-warning,frame-address,)
 KBUILD_CFLAGS	+= $(call cc-disable-warning, format-truncation)
 KBUILD_CFLAGS	+= $(call cc-disable-warning, format-overflow)
 KBUILD_CFLAGS	+= $(call cc-disable-warning, address-of-packed-member)
+KBUILD_CFLAGS	+= $(call cc-disable-warning, dangling-pointer)
 
 ifdef CONFIG_CC_OPTIMIZE_FOR_PERFORMANCE
 KBUILD_CFLAGS += -O2
